  "period_note": "Year-end position from NRB Bank Limited's own FY2021 Annual Report: Balance Sheet ('PROPERTY AND ASSETS' at line 5969, Total Assets 61,140,274,327, Total Shareholders' Equity 7,002,482,370 -- Paid-up 5,905,872,000 + Statutory reserve 786,381,698 + Other reserve 1,516,910 + Retained earnings 308,711,762, which sums exactly), and Basel III capital disclosure (CRAR 18.23%, Tier-2 1.39%, line 4534/4536). NRB Bank Securities PLC (the bank's brokerage subsidiary) was incorporated on 16 March 2021, so FY2021 is the last/first year for which a single (non-consolidated) Balance Sheet is presented -- FY2022 onward prints separate Consolidated and Solo statements. DISCREPANCY FOUND (material): the FY2022 report's own comparative column for 31 Dec 2021 shows Retained Earnings of 813,753,331 (equity 7,507,523,939) instead of this report's 308,711,762 (equity 7,002,482,370) -- a difference of exactly 505,041,569 -- while printing an unchanged Total Liabilities (54,139,901,192 vs this report's 54,137,791,957, a separate and immaterial ~2.1m difference). Because Total Liabilities was NOT adjusted to offset the equity change, the FY2022 report's own FY2021 comparative column does not balance (Total Liabilities + Equity = 61,647,425,131 versus its own stated Total Assets of 61,140,274,327, a 507.15m gap) -- i.e. the LATER report's comparative is the one that is internally inconsistent, while this FY2021 report's own figures balance exactly (54,137,791,957 + 7,002,482,370 = 61,140,274,327). Per the project's exception for arithmetically-impossible figures, the contemporaneous, internally-consistent FY2021 figures are used here.",
